# Every text file is LF — in the repo and in every working tree.
#
# Pinned rather than left to each machine's core.autocrlf because this repo is
# not just checked out, it is RSYNCED into consumer projects. Consumers run
# pre-commit hooks that normalize line endings to LF, so any CRLF reaching this
# repo reappears as drift in every consumer on every refresh, forever — the
# files show as modified, get normalized, and drift again on the next refresh.
#
# 15 files under skills/ui-ux-pro-max/ did exactly that until 2026-07-28
# (one, data/landing.csv, had genuinely mixed endings at 28/31 lines).
#
# Binary formats are matched explicitly below so `text=auto` never mangles them.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
